    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>New PCF hosting the multi-association review surface (reads task-015 provenance, writes ADR-024 regarding via PolymorphicResolverService, fires create-from-email actions); cross-cuts ADR-022 (PCF React 16 / platform libraries), ADR-024, ADR-015, ADR-003/008; FULL Step 9.5 gates required.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W4</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-17</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build a **Connections PCF** that hosts the multi-association review surface on the OOB `sprk_communication` model-driven form's right "accessories" column (the 34% side of the native 66/34 layout — the same column that already hosts the RELATED RECORD PCF). This REPLACES the Code-Page review surface (W4 architecture pivot, 2026-07-15 — see `notes/W4-architecture-pivot-oob-form-pcf.md`).

    An email is regarding MANY records at once (Matter + Organization + Contact + Invoice …, per ADR-024's regarding family and task-015's multi-field candidates). The PCF renders each typed association slot with its own suggestion + confidence + confirm/change, lets the user add missing dimensions, and offers "create from this email" actions (Event / To Do / Invoice) — some engine-suggested from the structural-detector signals (task 014).

    **Design source (do NOT redesign — port it):** the converged prototype `ConnectionsEditor` + `provenance.ts` at
    `src/client/code-pages/CommunicationPage/src/components/{ConnectionsEditor,provenance,CommunicationHeader}.tsx`
    (iterated live in `spaarke-prototype/projects/email-comm-r4-uat`). The chosen host is the right-rail (34%) layout. Port that component into the PCF's React root; keep the token-based Fluent v9 look (RegardingResolver already proves Fluent-v9-in-PCF on this form).

    On confirm/accept, write the chosen regarding via the EXISTING regarding machinery — `PolymorphicResolverService.applyResolverFields` (ADR-024 typed lookup + denormalized fields); set `sprk_associationstatus` → Resolved when all review slots are confirmed. Capture an override reason (feedback signal only, no learning loop). Add the "Communications Awaiting Association" Dataverse view (`sprk_associationstatus in (Suggested, Pending Review, Ambiguous)`, matter-level auth-scoped, ADR-003/008; AI-flagged privilege shown as a flag, never decided — ADR-015).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke PCF engineer. Expert on PCF lifecycle (init/updateView/destroy, ADR-022 platform libraries), Fluent v9 in PCF, the regarding family (`RegardingResolver`, `PolymorphicResolverService.applyResolverFields`, `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG`), and model-driven form control placement.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A deployable PCF bound to the `sprk_communication` form (right column) that: (1) reads `sprk_associationprovenance` (task-015 JSON) + `sprk_associationstatus` from the control context; (2) renders the multi-connection editor (typed slots, per-slot confidence band + confirm/change, Accept-all, Link-another, create-from-email actions with engine-suggested ones flagged) — ported from the prototype ConnectionsEditor; (3) on confirm, writes regarding via `PolymorphicResolverService.applyResolverFields` and advances status; (4) captures override reason as a feedback signal; (5) the "Communications Awaiting Association" view exists, auth-scoped. PCF prod-builds clean; no new regarding mechanism; Step 9.5 gates pass.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      W4 pivoted from a Code Page to enhancing the OOB form with PCFs (owner decision 2026-07-15). The OOB form already carries a Spaarke PCF (RELATED RECORD v1.4.6) in the right column; this is the next PCF there. The multi-association model matches the engine: task-015 provenance emits candidates across multiple regarding fields simultaneously; the PCF surfaces them as independent typed slots. Create-from-email actions tie to task-014 detector signals (invoice → Invoice, calendar-invite → Event, deadline-response → To Do) and foreshadow W5's CreateEvent/Task/Notification.
    </background>
