  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A PCF exists (`src/client/pcf/CommunicationConnections/`) bound to the `sprk_communication` form, prod-building via `npm run build:prod`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">It reads `sprk_associationprovenance` + status from context and renders the multi-slot connections editor (typed slots, per-slot confidence band + confirm/change, Accept-all, Link-another) ported from the prototype.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Confirm/Accept writes the chosen regarding via `PolymorphicResolverService.applyResolverFields` (grep confirms reuse; no new regarding mechanism) and advances `sprk_associationstatus`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">"Create from this email" actions render, with engine-suggested ones (from provenance signals) flagged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Override reason captured as a feedback signal (no learning loop invoked).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">"Communications Awaiting Association" view exists with the task-002-verified option-set integers, matter-level auth-scoped; privilege shown as a flag (ADR-015).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    W4 pivot (2026-07-15): OOB form + PCFs, not a Code Page. This PCF is the design-novel value; the composer + send/archival + attachment subgrid already exist (see the pivot note's capability audit). The prototype ConnectionsEditor is the converged UX — port it, don't redesign. Full create-and-link flows for Event/To Do may stub here and complete in W5 (CreateEvent/Task/Notification).

    Depends on task 015 (`sprk_associationprovenance` shape) + task 002 (option-set integers). Reuses the regarding family — extend the catalog if a target type is missing; add no new branches.
